The initial architecture and build/provisioning workflow are based on the
project conventions used by Krydix/ESPresso.

The protocol documentation is informed by public research from the Open
Wireless Link project and by inspection of the GPL-3.0-or-later OpenDrop and
OWL source trees. Any future source adapted from those projects must retain
its upstream copyright and license notices and identify its provenance.

`core/src/awdl_election.c` and
`core/include/espdrop/awdl_election.h` adapt the election algorithm from OWL
`src/election.c` and `src/election.h` at commit
`da255a70f221784c836d943dd3f243bc798f223b`. They retain the Open Wireless Link
Project and Milan Stute copyright notices and are licensed under
GPL-3.0-or-later.

archef2000/esp-owl is an important experimental ESP32-S3 reference. Its tree
does not currently contain a repository-level license, although individual
files carry GPL, MIT, Apache-2.0, and other notices. It is therefore kept out
of release firmware until its redistribution boundary is clarified.
